&lt;figure&gt;

&lt;img alt="A screenshot from GTA VI." data-caption="" data-portal-copyright="Image: Rockstar Games" data-has-syndication-rights="1" src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/06/ULTIMATE_EDITION_01_de9b57.jpg?quality=90&amp;#038;strip=all&amp;#038;crop=0,0,100,100" /&gt;
	&lt;figcaption&gt;
		&lt;/figcaption&gt;
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Arion Kurtaj, a member of the Lapsus$ cybercrime group who leaked 90 videos of &lt;em&gt;Grand Theft Auto VI&lt;/em&gt; in 2022 and hacked other big companies, pleaded guilty on Monday, according to the &lt;a href="https://www.cps.gov.uk/london-south/news/lapsus-hacker-who-leaked-gta-vi-gameplay-videos-convicted"&gt;UK's Crown Prosecution Service&lt;/a&gt; (CPS).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Kurtaj, who is now 21, hacked BT/EE sometime between August and November 2021, and starting in early November of that year, the company "noted a marked increase in unauthorised SIM swaps of their customers mobile phones." He was charged for those offenses and moved to a hotel for his "own protection" in September 2022, but "breached his bail conditions to carry out further hacks on major companies using a mobile phone, the h …&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.theverge.com/games/1035087/gta-vi-leaks-2022-hacker-pleads-guilty-arion-kurtaj"&gt;Read the full story at The Verge.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
						
									</description></item><item><title>Tech leaders are convinced that Jensen Huang’s exit was a plot against him</title><link>https://www.theverge.com/tech/1035027/tech-leaders-nvidia-jensen-huang-theories</link><guid>https://www.theverge.com/?p=1035027</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:17:34 -0500</pubDate><description>
											

						
&lt;figure&gt;

&lt;img alt="A photo of Jensen Huang" data-caption="" data-portal-copyright="Photo by Joel Saget / AFP via Getty Images" data-has-syndication-rights="1" src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/gettyimages-2299645290.jpg?quality=90&amp;#038;strip=all&amp;#038;crop=0,0,100,100" /&gt;
	&lt;figcaption&gt;
		&lt;/figcaption&gt;
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Jensen Huang's stunning resignation from Nvidia after more than 33 years has sent shockwaves throughout the tech industry. Now prominent figures are calling for Huang's reinstatement, and many are also hopping on board with a theory spreading throughout Silicon Valley: that the scandal is the result of a plot against the former CEO.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;At the center of this theory is the &lt;a href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/10/technology/alice-huang-megaspeed-nvidia-jensen-huang.html"&gt;reporting from &lt;em&gt;The&lt;/em&gt; &lt;em&gt;New York Times&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; that former Megaspeed executive Alice Huang, one of multiple women Huang is accused of having an affair with, is a Chinese spy. &lt;a href="https://www.reuters.com/world/china/us-justice-department-has-not-concluded-alice-huang-was-chinese-spy-blanche-says-2026-11-12/"&gt;US agencies haven't confirmed&lt;/a&gt; whether this is the case, and &lt;a href="https://www.theverge.com/tech/1030446/trump-jensen-huang-press-conference"&gt;President Donald Trump claims he was unaware&lt;/a&gt; of any spy …&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.theverge.com/tech/1035027/tech-leaders-nvidia-jensen-huang-theories"&gt;Read the full story at The Verge.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
						
									</description></item><item><title>United Airlines system outage disrupts departures just days after the big ground stop</title><link>https://www.theverge.com/transportation/1035025/united-airlines-outage-down-departures</link><guid>https://www.theverge.com/?p=1035025</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:54:59 -0500</pubDate><description>
											

						
