									</description></item><item><title>California sues OpenAI over rogue AI hacking incidents</title><link>https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/1034815/california-openai-hugging-face-lawsuit</link><guid>https://www.theverge.com/?p=1034815</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:46:01 -0500</pubDate><description>
											

						
&lt;figure&gt;

&lt;img alt="An illustration of the OpenAI logo." data-caption="" data-portal-copyright="Image: Cath Virginia / The Verge" data-has-syndication-rights="1" src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/10/STK155_OPEN_AI_4_CVirginia_D.png?quality=90&amp;#038;strip=all&amp;#038;crop=0,0,100,100" /&gt;
	&lt;figcaption&gt;
		&lt;/figcaption&gt;
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;California is suing OpenAI after its AI agents broke out of their testing environment and hacked other companies, including Hugging Face. In &lt;a href="https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/28912394-california-v-openai/"&gt;a lawsuit filed Monday&lt;/a&gt;, Attorney General &lt;a href="https://oag.ca.gov/news/press-releases/it%E2%80%99s-golden-state-not-wild-west-attorney-general-bonta-sues-openai-over"&gt;Rob Bonta accuses&lt;/a&gt; OpenAI of violating consumer safety law by knowingly developing a "dangerous product without proper oversight," &lt;a href="https://www.reuters.com/business/california-sues-openai-over-ai-models-cyberattacks-hugging-face-other-companies-2026-11-16/"&gt;as reported earlier by &lt;em&gt;Reuters&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;The lawsuit claims the cyberattack on Hugging Face "was the predictable result of an internal culture at OpenAI that prioritizes growth and rapid model development over safety and accountability." It alleges that OpenAI recently told the attorney general's office that it "lost control" of its AI agents  …&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/1034815/california-openai-hugging-face-lawsuit"&gt;Read the full story at The Verge.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
						
									</description></item><item><title>Sam Altman says he wants everyone ‘to have a lot of RAM’</title><link>https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/1034787/sam-altman-ram-shortage-semafor</link><guid>https://www.theverge.com/?p=1034787</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:41:28 -0500</pubDate><description>
											

						
&lt;figure&gt;

&lt;img alt="Sam Altman on a black background." data-caption="Sam… thank you. | Image: Getty Images" data-portal-copyright="Image: Getty Images" data-has-syndication-rights="1" src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/04/gettyimages-1778705436.jpg?quality=90&amp;#038;strip=all&amp;#038;crop=0,0,100,100" /&gt;
	&lt;figcaption&gt;
	Sam… thank you. | Image: Getty Images	&lt;/figcaption&gt;
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;OpenAI CEO Sam Altman is once again addressing his controversial comments on PC RAM purchases. "I want to be clear, I want people to have a lot of RAM, I think everybody should be able to buy a lot of RAM for their own computer," Altman said today. "I think the home tinkering is great."&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;The comments were &lt;a href="https://youtu.be/oi-E6xB4wSU?si=3J7vuvnU3rXPySvE&amp;amp;t=1192"&gt;made onstage&lt;/a&gt; at Semafor's &lt;a href="https://www.semafor.com/hub/semafor-silicon-valley-and-the-world-2026"&gt;Silicon Valley &amp;amp; The World&lt;/a&gt; summit on Monday.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Altman's remarks on RAM stirred up controversy last month. In an appearance &lt;a href="https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/1023820/sam-altman-ram-shortage-cloud-servers"&gt;on the &lt;em&gt;Cheeky Pint&lt;/em&gt; podcast&lt;/a&gt;, Altman said that it's "quite terrible" for everyone to have RAM in personal computers rather than in data centers. He later followed up on those comments in posts on  …&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/1034787/sam-altman-ram-shortage-semafor"&gt;Read the full story at The Verge.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
						
									</description></item><item><title>Some of our favorite PlayStation games are steeply discounted for Black Friday</title><link>https://www.theverge.com/gadgets/1034339/sony-black-friday-game-sale-2026-deals</link><guid>https://www.theverge.com/?p=1034339</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:36:14 -0500</pubDate><description>
											

						
